1. Standardized Interfaces: Components are designed with standardized connections or interfaces, allowing them to fit into a range of products seamlessly. This standardization is critical for ensuring that parts from different batches, models, or even different manufacturers can be used interchangeably.

2. Uniformity in Design: While individual components might perform different functions, their design incorporates uniform dimensions, fittings, and operational parameters. This uniformity ensures that one part can easily replace another without compatibility issues.

3. Simplicity and User-Friendly: The design aims to be user-friendly, enabling end-users to perform replacements or upgrades without requiring specialized tools or in-depth technical knowledge.